# Naban, Dean of Iteration judges the entering permanent as it is on the battlefield, continuous effects applied (CR 603.6a,
# 603.10; the rulings: "Look at each permanent as it exists on the battlefield, taking into account continuous effects"):
# Roaming Throne, a Golem, names Wizard as it enters and is a Wizard by its own static ability (layer 4), so its entering
# makes Aunt May trigger twice (24). Roaming Throne's own doubling reaches only Wizards, and Aunt May is none.
# Turn 1: the Plains pays Aunt May; Mox Sapphire and Mox Jet pay Naban, whose own entering gives two triggers (22).
# Turn 3: Black Lotus (any three) and Mox Sapphire pay Roaming Throne.

